                        "form": "paranomase"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4c4c6a90-958c-39d7-bcfd-6d0bfd6c5b75",
                        "entry_id": "fc9c59fe-8393-3b1f-9fbb-dd260a4d61a2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Rapprochement de mots aux sonorités proches, jouant ainsi sur la paronymie."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "rhetoric"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7b93df0a-a763-40f9-aeb5-ea9173304e3e",
                                "sense_id": "4c4c6a90-958c-39d7-bcfd-6d0bfd6c5b75",
                                "text": "Il y a une paronomase dans chacune des six phrases suivantes :"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f0b33a8a-a468-4760-83fd-22a78b3a9063",
                                "sense_id": "4c4c6a90-958c-39d7-bcfd-6d0bfd6c5b75",
                                "text": "Les phrases : « Je pars à l’île Maurice. Je pars à Lille, Maurice. » constituent une paronomase."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f035b6d6-b7f8-4bf8-b786-efaf18f0558c",
                                "sense_id": "4c4c6a90-958c-39d7-bcfd-6d0bfd6c5b75",
                                "text": "Il n'y pas d'hélice hélas. C'est là qu'est l'os"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "07b20440-ce4f-4f83-a5c0-b79484ac4a83",
                        "source_entry_id": "fc9c59fe-8393-3b1f-9fbb-dd260a4d61a2",
                        "source_sense_id": "4c4c6a90-958c-39d7-bcfd-6d0bfd6c5b75",
                        "target_lang_word": "Paronomasie",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "39309481-0c45-4a81-abbf-ff2568e6a9be",
                        "source_entry_id": "fc9c59fe-8393-3b1f-9fbb-dd260a4d61a2",
                        "source_sense_id": "4c4c6a90-958c-39d7-bcfd-6d0bfd6c5b75",
                        "target_lang_word": "paronomasia",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "paronomasia",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "76064f4a-0163-3ac8-8aaa-c78437388a49",
                                        "entry_id": "dbd12154-92d3-3316-8eaf-9234984f3b97",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A pun or play on words."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "rhetoric",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e837daf8-bc48-4b23-b041-ba1df61f794f",
                                                "sense_id": "76064f4a-0163-3ac8-8aaa-c78437388a49",
                                                "text": "Oh, by the way, any attempt to present me with any kind of testimonial will result in stern measures.\nAnd when I say stern measures, I am indulging in a paronomasia, or play on words! Good night."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ee876709-07de-4757-9add-d51e0927acf5",
                                                "sense_id": "76064f4a-0163-3ac8-8aaa-c78437388a49",
                                                "text": "Ev’rywhere but at Norfolk, where talk of Passion far outweighs its Enactment,– indeed, the Sailors’ paronomasia for that wretched Place,\nis ‘No-Fuck’."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9c0049c5-f31e-33c3-ad42-f71e25710ee9",
                                        "entry_id": "dbd12154-92d3-3316-8eaf-9234984f3b97",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The use of puns."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "rhetoric",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "343ce377-2454-47dd-926e-6e580253b2e6",
                                                "sense_id": "9c0049c5-f31e-33c3-ad42-f71e25710ee9",
                                                "text": "Paronomasia to the sense alludes,\nWhen words but little varied it includes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d6f256fc-5fe0-4383-9650-9f2ce99e5255",
                                                "sense_id": "9c0049c5-f31e-33c3-ad42-f71e25710ee9",
                                                "text": "[…] he gloomily regarded his new digital watch, faintly fascinated by the onward march of the square figures\nwhich turned one into the other with insolent ease, a kind of numerical paronomasia."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c0f10dae-c359-448f-85e3-39f6112df982",
                        "source_entry_id": "fc9c59fe-8393-3b1f-9fbb-dd260a4d61a2",
                        "source_sense_id": "4c4c6a90-958c-39d7-bcfd-6d0bfd6c5b75",
                        "target_lang_word": "agnominación",
                        "target_lang_code": "es",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "agnominación",
                                "target_lang_code": "es",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "465e5bc0-2fef-3dc5-a0b0-31a130197b56",
                                        "entry_id": "a1945fb6-eb4d-3532-9a80-03246687df61",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Figura o juego de palabras que consiste en combinar dentro de una frase o un párrafo vocablos con sonido similar pero significado diferente (parónimos)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "retórica"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "39d981c9-50f7-43f7-bc2d-03d1cbaeeada",
                                                "sense_id": "465e5bc0-2fef-3dc5-a0b0-31a130197b56",
                                                "text": "El poeta Blas de Otero crea la agnominación: \"un hombre a hombros del miedo\" en su poema."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8ad554cf-90b8-4dfc-a11e-a083800c54b0",
                                                "sense_id": "465e5bc0-2fef-3dc5-a0b0-31a130197b56",
                                                "text": "El poeta Octavio Paz crea numerosas agnominaciones en su libro «Libertad bajo palabra» (1949), por ejemplo: \"El erizo se irisa, se eriza, se riza de risa\"."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f87f38fd-167f-48fd-972b-d19ec5574a87",
                        "source_entry_id": "fc9c59fe-8393-3b1f-9fbb-dd260a4d61a2",
